// D1693 — a nullable LIST narrowed at the use site, then met by the index and `.length`
// floors. The un-annotated face of a delivery through a parameter is the monomorphization
// pin, and the pin re-asked those floors against the SUBSTITUTED type (`A[] | null`) rather
// than the narrowed one, so it refused what the annotated face runs.
//
// The hit branch carries both narrowing spellings, because they reach the floor by different
// routes: `!= null` is a flow fact the body collects, `?? []` is the operator's own result
// type. On master the first refuses `cannot index non-array A[] | null` and the second
// refuses the same sentence for a receiver whose type after `??` is `A[]`.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@SKIP@@
map_value: the builder already guards the read with `!= null`, so this TEST is a second null
compare on a value the first one narrowed — the refusal is the template's shape, not a floor
// @@PRELUDE@@
type A = { r: i32 }
function mkA(): A[] | null { return [{ r: 4 }] }
// @@VALUE@@
mkA()
// @@TYPE@@
A[] | null
// @@TEST@@
v != null
// @@HIT@@
print(v[0].r)
print(v.length)
const q = v ?? []
print(q.length)
// @@MISS@@
print(0)
// @@WANT@@
4 then 1 then 1
